                <pb facs="0660" n="566" xml:id="pg566"/>

                <head>No. 363.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hastings to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1886-12-27"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 27, 1886</date>.
                        (Received January 31, 1887.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 93.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that on the 22d
                    instant, Hon. John E. Bush was commissioned by His Majesty the King as minister
                    plenipotentiary to the Kings of Samoa and Tonga, and the independent chiefs and
                    peoples of Polynesia.”</p>
                <p>Mr. Bush is a half-caste Hawaiian of considerable ability, a member of the house
                    of nobles and at one time a member of the cabinet as minister of interior.</p>
                <p>He left here for Samoa on the 26th instant, taking with him a secretary of
                    legation and two attaches.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank P.
                    Hastings.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
